
* Diode SPICE subcircuit
* Generic diode model with proper SPICE parameters
*
* Parameters:
*   IS - Saturation current (controls forward voltage)
*   N - Ideality factor (1.0 for ideal diode, higher for real diodes)
*   RS - Series resistance
*   CJO - Junction capacitance (optional)
*
* Nodes:
*   1 - Anode
*   2 - Cathode

* Standard silicon diode - ~0.7V forward voltage
.SUBCKT D 1 2 PARAMS: IS=1e-14 N=1.0 RS=10m CJO=1p
D1 1 2 DMODEL
.MODEL DMODEL D(IS={IS} N={N} RS={RS} CJO={CJO})
.ENDS D

* Schottky diode variant - ~0.3V forward voltage, higher leakage
.SUBCKT D_Schottky 1 2 PARAMS: IS=1e-8 N=1.2 RS=5m CJO=2p
D1 1 2 SCHOTTKY_MODEL
.MODEL SCHOTTKY_MODEL D(IS={IS} N={N} RS={RS} CJO={CJO})
.ENDS D_Schottky

* Zener diode variant - includes breakdown behavior
.SUBCKT D_Zener 1 2 PARAMS: IS=1e-14 N=1.0 RS=10m BV=5.1 IBV=5m CJO=1p
D1 1 2 ZENER_MODEL
.MODEL ZENER_MODEL D(IS={IS} N={N} RS={RS} BV={BV} IBV={IBV} CJO={CJO})
.ENDS D_Zener
XD1 BUZ_N V5 D IS=1e-14 N=1.0 RS=10m CJO=1p
* MMBT3904 (2N3904 die) Gummel-Poon model, Fairchild/onsemi published parameters.
.subckt MMBT3904_SUB C B E
Q1 C B E QMMBT3904
.model QMMBT3904 NPN (IS=6.734f XTI=3 EG=1.11 VAF=74.03 BF=416.4 NE=1.259 ISE=6.734f IKF=66.78m XTB=1.5
+ BR=.7371 NC=2 ISC=0 IKR=0 RC=1 CJC=3.638p MJC=.3085 VJC=.75 FC=.5 CJE=4.493p MJE=.2593 VJE=.75
+ TR=239.5n TF=301.2p ITF=.4 VTF=4 XTF=2 RB=10)
.ends MMBT3904_SUB
XQ1 BUZ_N BUZ_B GND MMBT3904_SUB 
* Resistor SPICE subcircuit
* Model with parasitic series inductance and parallel capacitance
*
* Equivalent circuit:
*
*              ┌── Cp ──┐
*   1 ── ESL ──┤        ├── 2
*              └── R ───┘
*
* Behavior:
*   f << SRF: Z ≈ R (purely resistive)
*   f ~ SRF:  Parallel resonance of L and Cp; impedance peaks for low R,
*             dips for high R
*   f >> SRF: Cp dominates (capacitive roll-off)
*
* Parameters:
*   RVAL - Resistance value in ohms
*   ESL  - Parasitic series inductance (henries)
*   CP   - Parasitic parallel capacitance (farads)

.SUBCKT R 1 2 PARAMS: RVAL=1k ESL=0.5n CP=0.05p
L_esl 1 mid {ESL}
R1 mid 2 {RVAL}
C_p mid 2 {CP}
.ENDS R
XR1 BUZZER BUZ_B R RVAL=1k ESL=700p CP=80f
XR2 BUZ_B GND R RVAL=10k ESL=700p CP=80f


V_5V V5 GND DC 5
* active buzzer: ~30 mA at 5 V with a magnetic transducer coil (worst case 10 mH)
R_BZ V5 BZ_INT 160
L_BZ BZ_INT BUZ_N 10m
* ESP32-S3 GPIO (3.3 V, ~25 Ohm output) beeps for 2 ms
V_GPIO GP GND PULSE(0 3.3 1m 20n 20n 2m 10m)
R_GPIO GP BUZZER 25
.control
  tran 1u 6m
  meas tran ib_on FIND i(V_GPIO) AT=2.9m
  meas tran vce_on FIND v(BUZ_N) AT=2.9m
  let ic = (5 - v(BUZ_N))/160
  meas tran vkick_peak MAX v(BUZ_N) FROM=3m TO=4m
  meas tran vbuz_n_idle FIND v(BUZ_N) AT=0.9m
.endc
